1. Definitions

"Software" means the ZZ Board code, project documentation, and original
visual assets distributed under this license, including project screenshots,
icons, built-in Skins, and permitted modifications. Third-party components,
third-party assets, and user content outside these project materials remain
subject to their own rights and licenses.

"Licensor" means each copyright holder to the extent that holder has the
authority to grant the rights stated here. "You" means the person or legal
entity exercising those rights.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form of the Software for making
modifications, including the modifications, build scripts, dependency
manifests and lockfiles, and instructions needed to build the distributed
version. It excludes users' data, credentials, signing keys, proprietary
development tools, and independently available general-purpose tools.

"Internal Use" means use by You and Your personnel for Your own work,
including business work, without providing the Software as a product or
hosted service to external customers.

"Core Charge" means a mandatory payment, subscription, paid membership,
required donation, or other consideration required to obtain the Software,
use it, unlock its capabilities, or access a hosted replacement of it. A
charge for a bundle whose substantial value is access to the Software is a
Core Charge, regardless of the label used for that charge. Optional
services that do not condition access to the Software are not Core Charges.

"Replacement Hosting" means operating the Software or a modification for
external users as a substantially substitutable board, note, or Codex
project-review service. A charge for access to such a service is a Core
Charge. Free community hosting with optional sponsorship is not prohibited
Replacement Hosting under this license.

2. Grant

Subject to this license, each Licensor grants You a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free right to read, use, reproduce, modify, build,
display, and distribute the Software and modifications in source and
binary forms for the permitted uses in Section 3. These rights are not
limited to non-business users.

3. Permitted uses

You may use and modify the Software for personal use and Internal Use,
including paid employment and business work. You may publish community
Forks, distribute the original or modified source and binaries free of
Core Charges, and operate free community hosting. You may accept voluntary
donations or sponsorship that do not condition access or features.

You may charge independently for training, installation, configuration,
support, data migration, maintenance, or consulting, provided customers
can obtain and use the Software without buying those services. You may
develop an integration for Your own Internal Use. Offering Software as a
substantial part of a paid external product remains subject to Section 4.

4. Restricted uses

Without separate written permission from the relevant rights holders, You
must not impose a Core Charge, resell or sublicense the Software as paid
software, sell a modified edition or paid feature access, or offer paid
Replacement Hosting. Repackaging the Software in a bundle, advertising a
payment as support when it is required for software access, or making only
a reduced edition free does not avoid this restriction.

This restriction does not prohibit free community Forks that substitute
for the official application, Internal Use, or the optional services and
sponsorship expressly allowed in Section 3. Ordinary communication with
an independent paid API does not itself turn Your private Internal Use
into prohibited Replacement Hosting.

5. Distribution conditions

Every distribution of the Software or a modification must retain this
license, applicable copyright and attribution notices, third-party
notices, and a clear statement of material modifications. Modified
distributions must identify their maintainer and distinguish themselves
from the official ZZ Board project; factual attribution is permitted.

You must license Your modifications to the Software under this same
license when distributing them. You may not impose terms that remove
recipients' rights granted by this license or bypass its restrictions.
This condition does not relicense independent third-party components.

When distributing a binary, You must provide its Corresponding Source
under this same license, either alongside the binary or through a
clearly identified, freely accessible link to the exact matching source.
If You use a link, keep it available for at least as long as You make
the binary available. A link to a moving branch or a different version
does not satisfy this requirement. No source publication is required
for modifications that are used only internally and not distributed.

